title: L1_01_Description
tags: 
colorID: 8
position: -1651,-197
---
<<PlayYarnAmbient DialogueCustomCommands yarnambient01>>
<<setPicture DialogueCustomCommands 01_descent>>
The air smells like a typical cave - moisture and cold seep in through the crater above you. However, there is no doubt that this is not a natural cavern.
-> ...
The huge concrete hall looks like an underground terminal of an airport or train station. You are apparently on the main entrance level of some huge underground installation.
-> Look around.
It's dark, but not completely. Judging from what looks like faint emergency lighting, there's still power in the grid. After so many years?
-> So this was originally the way in?
Yes. Large vault door, security gates, conveyor belts, and a cargo bay at the far end. This was the way in and out of the vault.
-> Look up.
<<setPicture DialogueCustomCommands 01_hole>>
When you look up, you can see how the ceiling was destroyed by whatever made the opening you came through.
-> ...
The layer of concrete is so thick you can now barely see the sky above.
-> Move on...
===
title: L1_01B_Vault_Door
tags: 
colorID: 8
position: -1363,-193
---
<<setPicture DialogueCustomCommands 01_vault_door>>
The large armored doors leading outside are closed.
-> ...
You can't recognize this technology, but you're able to understand its principle of working. Huge, armored, probably ceramic doors are closed with a complicated hydraulic mechanism leaving no doubt...
-> ...
...they won't budge.
-> ...
This place would have stayed sealed forever if not for the breach above you...
-> Come closer...
Underneath the vault doors you can see a pile of... bodies?
