title: L8_Intranet_message
tags: 
colorID: 0
position: 10597,47
---
Hello, dr. Steinfeld? This is Emma Shulz from the Infirmary.
-> ...
I can't reach you on the comms, so I'm leaving this message.
-> ...
We're having patients with very unusual symptoms. The first one came by himself in the morning, complaining about a headache.
-> ...
After an hour he became aggressive (screamed something about butterflies) so I gave him a shot of benzodiazepine.
-> ...
His skin is sticky as tar and his EEG and ECG are giving some crazy results.
-> ...
I don't have the means to do proper research, and I already have 7 patients with this kind of symptoms. 
-> ...
The last two were dragged here by security.|I need professional assistance.
-> ...
Please call me.
[[Check files|L8_Patient_file]]
===
title: L8_Patient_file
tags: 
colorID: 0
position: 10870,40
---
--------------|Subject Record: Kogler, Victor|Filed: Jan 14, 2041|By: Ada Shulz||Status: LIVING|--------------
-> ...
The patient's body produces abnormal amount of stem cells. Main organs started to grow and change shape.
-> ...
Also, the man's muscle tissue has increased in volume several times. Also stem cells?
-> ...
Comment: Brief analysis suggests that patient's aggression and unusual strength may be the effect of the body's mutation.
-> ...
We need more research and better equipment to understand what happened. I tried to contact dr. Steinfeld but with no luck.
-> ...
The whole hospital level is out of reach. Network error again?
[[Check messages|L8_Intranet_message]]
===
title: L9_02_Terminal_last_message
tags: 
colorID: 8
position: 12005,-245
---
You found a working terminal in the chef's office.
-> Read the logs
You can access the last conversation made with this terminal.|The date reads: Jan 13, 2041
-> View
Karl Spiegel: Are we still on for bridge tonight?
-> ...
Jens Kissling: I can't, something happened at the reactor core last night. They're calling in all the staff. Even me.
-> ...
Karl Spiegel: They can't replace a light bulb by themselves? Come on man, you're almost 70! I'm surprised they're aware you're still alive.
-> ...
Jens Kissling: This is serious Karl. Remember the millennium bug? When the reactor malfunctioned?
-> ...
Karl Spiegel: Of course I remember, it was only 40 years ago ;)
-> ...
Jens Kissling: Find a power generator and as much gasoline you can.
-> ...
Karl Spiegel: Are you serious?
-> ...
Jens Kissling: I don't know, but be ready for the worst.
-> ...
Karl Spiegel: OK
-> ...
Jens Kissling: and Karl...
-> ...
Karl Spiegel: yes?
-> ...
Jens Kissling: not a word. to anyone.
-> ...
Karl Spiegel: you know me.
-> ...
Jens Kissling: stay safe.
[[Leave the terminal|L9_Exit]]
